      "id": 146928,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-28T03:53:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Let's see. &nbsp;Wraith has a mansion, and would favor dark colors. &nbsp;Tachyon would have at least one, but probably two or more playrooms filled with scientific toys to mess with. &nbsp;I'm also kind of imagining that her wife would have a large hand in decorating the rest of the house. &nbsp;I'd expect Legacy's house to feel very 'ordinary middle class family'. &nbsp;Also, we've got a picture of what their kitchen looks like on Next Evolution, although considering what that evolution was, it wouldn't surprise me if their kitchen needed a bit of a remodel after that. &nbsp;I imagine that Legacy would have converted his garage or basement into a gym. &nbsp;Bunker would also have some sort of exercise apparatus, and probably some tools and things in the garage. &nbsp;As far as I know he's a bachelor, so it would be pretty small. &nbsp;Absolute Zero's house would be very austere and empty, and probably also fairly small.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(Note: &nbsp;I don't know how neighborhood layouts work in the Sims, so I'm assuming that they're all in a row)</p><p>I'd probably put AZ on one end since he's standoffish, and Wraith on the other (partially because mansions go on the ends of rows and partially because she's fairly quiet as well), with Legacy in the middle. &nbsp;I'm leaning towards putting Tachyon near AZ rather than Wraith, since it would be good to have her on hand in case his equipment breaks down, and she would happily ignore his grumpiness, and Wraith wouldn't want to put up with her hyperactivity. &nbsp;On the other hand, Wraith seems closer to Legacy than any of the others, so maybe put his house next to hers, then Tachyon's (so the two wives could hang out while their significant others are out superheroing), and that leaves Bunker and then AZ, putting the two single guys adjecent.</p>",
